  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the top government contractors by contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The page total of obligations is $10.5B. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP leads the list with obligations of $900M, followed by TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC with obligations of $875M and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with obligations of $633M. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC holds obligations of $550M, while CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC has obligations of $489M. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC, HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC, UT-BATTELLE LLC, and PANTEXAS DETERRENCE, LLC complete the top ten with obligations of $379M, $373M, $323M, $302M, and $281M respectively. The list shows which entities received the largest shares of contract obligations during the fiscal year to date. Agencies and contractors can use the ranking to identify major obligation recipients and compare peers by exact obligation amounts reported here.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who received the most obligations so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received the most obligations with $900M. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC follow with $875M and $633M respectively. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC round out the next positions with $550M and $489M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does the page total represent?",
        "body": "The page total represents the sum of contract obligations reported for FY2027 to date, equal to $10.5B. The total is a fiscal year to date figure, so current-year totals are partial. The ranking lists each contractor with its reported obligations for comparison."
      }
    ]
  },
